      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "This sets `permissions: contents: read` on the CI workflow, which is all the jobs use.\n\nOn this repository the token is already read-only, through the repository's default. The workflow's `permissions` key then adjusts that default ([GitHub docs](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/workflow-syntax#how-permissions-are-calculated-for-a-workflow-job)), so the setting now lives in the workflow and also holds in forks, where each owner sets the default.\n\nThe same change for libsecp256k1 is bitcoin-core/secp256k1#1964.\n\nCloses #36512.\n",
    "labels": [
      {
