      "body": "> Nothing is exploitable today: on this repository the token is already read-only\r\n\r\nCan you please refer to the official docs as to why the token is already read-only and why this change is needed? Your description sounds plausible, but it would be good to have the official docs.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> and adds `persist-credentials: false` to every `actions/checkout` step, so the token no longer stays in `.git/config` for later steps to read.\r\n\r\nSeems a bit verbose and mostly irrelevant, as the token is read-only? I'd say to drop this change to keep the yaml slim.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> Pinning actions by hash is left out, after #35754 and the discussion in #36512.\r\n\r\nI think it is enough if the pull just lists the stuff it does. Listing all the stuff it doesn't do seems unrelated.",
